# Right On Time: settings for your own copy (SPECIFICATIONS section 11.1).
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Every other setting has an own-copy default, so this file holds only the one value a copy needs.
# Docker Compose reads it with:  docker compose --env-file .env -f infra/compose.yaml ...
#
# SAMPLE_PASSWORD_SEED makes the password of each sample person (the first 10 characters of a code
# worked out from this seed and the person's email). It needs 16 or more characters.
#
# This value is PUBLISHED. It is not a secret: it opens only the made-up people of a copy on your
# own computer. The hosted demo uses a different, private value that is never in this repository.
# Do not use this value for anything that holds real data. Change it before setup if you want
# different sample passwords. Setup writes the passwords once, so change it before the first setup.
SAMPLE_PASSWORD_SEED=right-on-time-sample-seed-2026
